# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the test suite.
#
# SurrealDB's async runtime keeps worker threads alive past the end of main().
# LeakSanitizer takes its snapshot at process exit, so whatever those threads
# still hold is reported as leaked. The give-away is the stack: every frame is
# `asan_thread_start` plus Rust allocator internals, with no test-suite or
# surrealdb_c frame anywhere.
#
# Measured on the Auth group (which hashes a password via crypto::argon2 and so
# does the most background work): 3/12 runs before the 0.2.1 geometry fix,
# 2/12 after -- unchanged, and unrelated to it. A gate that fails one run in six
# gets ignored, which is worse than not having one.
#
# Cost, stated plainly: this also hides a genuine leak that originates on a
# worker thread. That is tolerable only because the Rust staticlib is not
# instrumented anyway, so such a leak would have no useful frames either way.
# Anything allocated on the main path -- which is all of the C API surface --
# is still caught.
leak:asan_thread_start
